# Ledger for test/diff_compiler_prelude_shadow_census.sh (#2153, S-shadow-census-gate).
#
# One row per top-level standalone function exported from stdlib/core.mdk,
# `name|verdict`, where verdict is the CURRENT MEASURED outcome of the probe:
#
#   interface Ifc c where
#     <name> : c -> Int
#   impl Ifc Int where
#     <name> v = v
#   main = println (<name> 1)
#
# driven through `check`, `run`, and `build` (+ executing the built binary).
#
#   PASS                -- check/run/build all ACCEPT and both run's stdout
#                          and the built binary's stdout print exactly `1`
#                          (S1-PRELUDE (a): the interface method wins and the
#                          program builds, docs/spec/SHADOW-SEMANTICS.md).
#   FAIL_BUILD           -- check and run ACCEPT (run prints `1`), but build
#                          exits 1: `runtime error [E-PANIC]: unbound method:
#                          <name>` -- #2153's class, the gate this slice ships
#                          to make objectively measurable.
#   SPECIAL_RUN_REJECT   -- `println` only: the probe template itself calls
#                          `println (...)`, so shadowing `println` makes the
#                          OUTER call resolve through the shadow too, and
#                          `run` rejects while `build` still accepts and
#                          prints `1`. Not part of the #2153 family; kept as
#                          its own bucket rather than folded into either of
#                          the other two, per the packet's own note that
#                          `println` is special-cased.
#
# THIS LEDGER IS THE RATCHET: a PASS row that regresses to anything else is a
# gate failure, full stop -- see the gate's own header for how a name moving
# the OTHER direction (e.g. a slice 2-5 fix flipping FAIL_BUILD -> PASS) is
# handled (re-pin this row, on purpose, in that slice's own diff).
#
# Names are derived from stdlib/core.mdk at gate-run time (never hand-copied
# from #2153's issue body) -- the gate's own coverage self-audit fails loudly
# if a name here has vanished from core.mdk, or a core.mdk standalone is
# missing from this ledger (a NEW prelude function ships with no ledger row).
#
# Measured 2026-08-28, cold-built binary, this worktree: 57 standalone names,
# 34 PASS / 22 FAIL_BUILD / 1 SPECIAL_RUN_REJECT. #2153's issue body claims
# "33 pass / 23 fail / println special" -- this ledger's numbers are the
# derived truth, one name off in each direction from the issue's prose
# count; see the sprint report for which name moved.
all|FAIL_BUILD
and|PASS
any|FAIL_BUILD
apply|PASS
arbitraryList|PASS
arbitraryString|FAIL_BUILD
clamp|FAIL_BUILD
compose|PASS
const|PASS
count|PASS
curry|PASS
discard|FAIL_BUILD
elem|FAIL_BUILD
filterThen|FAIL_BUILD
find|PASS
flatMap|PASS
flat|PASS
flip|PASS
foldThen|FAIL_BUILD
forEach|FAIL_BUILD
fromOption|FAIL_BUILD
fromResult|FAIL_BUILD
fromResultOr|PASS
fst|PASS
guard|PASS
identity|FAIL_BUILD
isErr|PASS
isEven|PASS
isNone|PASS
isOdd|PASS
isOk|PASS
isSome|PASS
map2|FAIL_BUILD
map3|FAIL_BUILD
mapErr|FAIL_BUILD
maximum|PASS
minimum|PASS
neq|FAIL_BUILD
notElem|PASS
not|FAIL_BUILD
on|FAIL_BUILD
or|PASS
otherwise|FAIL_BUILD
pipe|PASS
println|SPECIAL_RUN_REJECT
print|PASS
product|PASS
repeatThen|FAIL_BUILD
replaceWith|PASS
runEach|FAIL_BUILD
snd|PASS
